OL,3,GNEWSACancelled GWR trains 'least bad
OL,4,Achoice'
OL,5,
OL,6,FCampaigners say the cancellation of
OL,7,Ffive weekday services between Penzance
OL,8,Fin Cornwall and Plymouth or Exeter in
OL,9,FDevon has been "the least bad choice"
OL,10,Ffor operator GWR to get on top of
OL,11,Freliability problems with its newer
OL,12,FClass 175 fleet locally.
OL,14,FRoger Blake, national director at
OL,15,Fcampaigning group Railfuture, said
OL,16,Ftemporary cancellations from Monday
OL,17,Fwere "an unfortunate step back in order
OL,18,Fto then, we hope, take a couple of
OL,19,Fsteps forward".
OL,23,APub: 07-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
